problems.problem:
Find a set $S = \{n\}$ of $7$ consecutive positive integers for which a polynomial $P(x)$ of the $5$th degree exists with the following properties:
(a) all the coefficients in $P(x)$ are integers;
(b) $P(n) = n$ for $5$ members of $S$, including the least and greatest;
(c) $P(n) = 0$ for one member of $S$.
